<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Moctezuma II</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1466–<a href="/years/1520">1520</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Moctezuma II was ruler of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aztec-empire">Aztec Empire</a> from 1502 to 1520. He expanded the empire and centralised power, but faced the arrival of Hernan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/corte">Cortes</a> in 1519. Taken captive by the Spanish, he died in 1520 during the upheavals that preceded the fall of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tenochtitlan">Tenochtitlan</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/moctezuma-ii.jpg" alt="Moctezuma II" width="261" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Moctezuma_Mendoza.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
